.TH TMUX-WORKSPACE-RESUME-RESUMERS 7 "October 2026" "tmux-workspace-resume 0.2.0" "Miscellaneous"
.SH NAME
tmux-workspace-resume-resumers \- how tmux-workspace-resume relaunches the program that ran in a pane
.SH DESCRIPTION
When
.BR tmux-workspace-resume (1)
saves a snapshot it runs every
.I resumer
against every pane. A resumer is an executable that looks at the pane (its shell's pid, working
directory and foreground command) and either claims it, printing the command that brings the
program back, or passes. Resumers are tried in name order; the first claim wins.
.SH LOCATIONS
.TP
.I /usr/share/tmux-workspace-resume/resumers/
Shipped resumers.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tmux-workspace-resume/resumers/
User resumers. A file with the same name as a shipped one replaces it; a new name adds one.
Names start with two digits that fix the order, e.g.
.IR 15\-codex .
.SH SHIPPED RESUMERS
.TP
.B 10-claude
Claude Code registers every interactive process in
.I ~/.claude/sessions/<pid>.json
together with the tmux pane it runs in. The resumer finds the record for the pane, checks that
the pid still belongs to that process, and emits
.B claude \-\-resume
.I session-id
with the conversation's directory. Two Claude panes in the same directory therefore come back as
two different conversations. A Claude without a record (started seconds ago, or an older
version) is relaunched with the command line it was started with, which starts a new
conversation rather than guessing one with
.BR \-\-continue .
.TP
.B 20-ssh
Claims a pane whose foreground command is
.B ssh
and whose shell has an
.B ssh
child; emits that child's exact command line. Transports started by git, scp or rsync are not
direct children of the shell and are left alone.
.TP
.BR 30-codex ", " 40-gemini ", " 50-copilot
OpenAI Codex CLI, Google Gemini CLI and GitHub Copilot CLI do not record their tmux pane. These
resumers find the agent's process under the pane's shell (also when it runs as
.BR node " <script>" )
and identify its session by, in order: a session file the process holds open
.RI ( ~/.codex/sessions/.../rollout-*.jsonl ,
.IR ~/.gemini/tmp/<hash>/chats/session-* ,
.IR ~/.copilot/session-state/<uuid>/ );
the session id on its command line
.RB ( \-\-resume " <id> or " resume " <id>,"
which is how a restore relaunches it);
the session created soonest after the process started in the process's directory, or for a
resumed session the most recently modified one; and, failing that, the command line the agent
was started with. They emit
.BR "codex resume " <id> ,
.BR "gemini \-\-resume " <id>
and
.BR "copilot \-\-resume " <id> .
Two new agents started in one directory within the same second cannot be told apart. Written from
the published formats, not verified against the real binaries.
.TP
.B 90-whitelist
Claims a pane whose foreground job consists of programs named in the
.B RESUME_COMMANDS
setting and emits its command line: a single command or a pipeline, also when it was started
from a nested shell.
.BI "sudo " program
is matched by
.IR program .
A job with its standard input or output redirected is not claimed, since the redirection
cannot be read back. A serial device on the command line is replaced by its
.I /dev/serial/by\-id/
link, which survives the renumbering of
.IR ttyUSB *
and
.IR ttyACM *
devices across reboots. Without such a job, a listed direct child of the shell (a suspended
editor) is claimed.
.SH CONTRACT
A resumer is invoked as
.B <resumer> probe
with these variables in the environment:
.TP
.B TWR_PANE_ID
The tmux pane id, e.g.
.IR %38 .
.TP
.B TWR_PANE_PID
Pid of the pane's shell; the program is normally a direct child.
.TP
.B TWR_WINDOW_ID
.TP
.B TWR_SESSION
.TP
.B TWR_CWD
The pane's current directory.
.TP
.B TWR_COMMAND
The pane's foreground command as tmux reports it
.RI ( #{pane_current_command} ).
.TP
.BI TWR_ KEY
Every configuration key, e.g.
.BR TWR_RESUME_COMMANDS .
.TP
.B TWR_HOME
The installation directory;
.I $TWR_HOME/lib/common.sh
can be sourced for helpers such as
.BR shell_quote ,
.B proc_cmdline_to_shell
and
.BR children_of ,
and
.I $TWR_HOME/lib/agents.sh
for
.BR agent_find_process ,
.BR agent_resume_arg ,
.B agent_pick
and
.B agent_emit
(see the shipped agent resumers).
.PP
To claim the pane the resumer exits 0 and prints one JSON object:
.PP
.nf
  {"cmd": "claude --resume 12345678-...", "cwd": "/home/me/proj", "meta": {...}}
.fi
.PP
.B cmd
is typed into the restored pane's shell after
.BI "cd " cwd
(default: the pane's directory) and must therefore be shell-safe; use
.B shell_quote
or
.BR proc_cmdline_to_shell .
.B meta
is stored in the snapshot for display and debugging. Exit 1 passes the pane on to the next
resumer. Any other exit status, output that is not JSON, or more than 5 seconds of runtime is
logged and treated as a pass.
.PP
.B <resumer> info
prints a one-line description for
.BR "tmux-workspace-resume resumers" .
.SH EXAMPLE
A resumer for a program that is restarted with the same arguments:
.PP
.nf
  #!/usr/bin/env bash
  set -euo pipefail
  . "$TWR_HOME/lib/common.sh"
  case ${1:-} in
    info) echo "myprog: restart with the same arguments"; exit 0 ;;
    probe) ;;
    *) exit 2 ;;
  esac
  for child in $(children_of "$TWR_PANE_PID"); do
    [ "$(proc_argv0 "$child")" = myprog ] || continue
    jq -cn --arg cmd "$(proc_cmdline_to_shell "$child")" '{cmd: $cmd, meta: {}}'
    exit 0
  done
  exit 1
.fi
.PP
Try it on a live pane with
.B tmux-workspace-resume resumers probe
.IR %id .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux-workspace-resume (1)
